OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARegulating AI 'not the right place to
OL,4,Astart' says Bailey
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Governor of the Bank of England has
OL,7,Fsaid regulating artificial intelligence
OL,8,F(AI) "is not the right place to start"
OL,9,Fbut instead called first for "rigorous"
OL,10,Ftesting to find vulnerabilities and
OL,11,Fsafeguards to contain risk.
OL,13,FWriting his first-ever article for
OL,14,FSubstack, Andrew Bailey said the risks
OL,15,Faround AI were "real and increasingly
OL,16,Fsignificant".
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790777930
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARegulating AI 'not the right place to
OL,4,Astart' says Bailey
OL,5,
OL,6,FBailey said the development of AI
OL,7,Fshould not be halted or prohibited -
OL,8,F"on the contrary, the benefits are
OL,9,Fimmense" - but added there must be a
OL,10,Fsystem for intervention and to
OL,11,Festablish boundaries in which AI
OL,12,Foperates.
OL,14,FIn recent weeks, the debate about the
OL,15,Fpotential risks surrounding the rapid
OL,16,Fdevelopment of AI and what it means for
OL,17,Fhumanity has intensified.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/19
